Core Engine
The foundational layer that bootstraps and orchestrates all immersive subsystems.

1.1 Initialization Sequence
Theme Detection: Identifies whether the current page uses the immersive layout variant
Capability Checks: Verifies WebGL support, device performance tier, and viewport dimensions
Module Loader: Dynamically imports required subsystems based on page configuration
Event Bus: Centralized pub/sub system for cross-module communication
1.2 Configuration Registry
Stores theme-specific settings (animation speeds, easing curves, breakpoints)
Exposes a unified API for section-level overrides
Supports runtime mutation for A/B testing and personalization
1.3 Lifecycle Manager
Handles mount/unmount of immersive sections
Coordinates with Shopify's Section Rendering API for lazy loading
Manages cleanup of GPU resources on section removal
3D Rendering Pipeline
The WebGL-based rendering stack responsible for all visual output.

2.1 Renderer
WebGL Context: Created with alpha, antialias, and powerPreference: "high-performance"
Pixel Ratio: Clamped to a maximum of 2.0 to balance quality and performance
Clear Color: Transparent to allow CSS background layering
Output Encoding: sRGB for correct color reproduction
2.2 Scene Graph
Root Scene: Single shared scene for all immersive content
Section Nodes: Each immersive section attaches as a child node
Layer Ordering: Z-depth management for overlapping editorial and 3D content
2.3 Render Loop
RequestAnimationFrame: Driven by display refresh rate
Delta Time: Frame-independent animation timing
Conditional Rendering: Pauses when tab is hidden or section is off-screen
Double Buffering: Prevents visual tearing during updates
2.4 Post-Processing
Bloom: Adds glow to emissive materials and highlights
Tone Mapping: ACES filmic tone mapping for HDR-to-LDR conversion
Anti-Aliasing: FXAA or SMAA pass for edge smoothing
Color Grading: LUT-based color correction per section
Camera System
Manages the virtual camera that defines the viewer's perspective.

3.1 PerspectiveCamera
Field of View (FOV): Dynamically adjusted based on viewport aspect ratio
Near/Far Planes: Configured to match scene depth requirements
Aspect Ratio: Updated on window resize events
Projection Matrix: Recalculated on any parameter change
3.2 Camera Controller
Scroll-Driven Position: Camera position maps directly to scroll progress
Path Animation: Camera follows predefined spline paths through the scene
Look-At Target: Optional target tracking for focused viewing
Smooth Damping: Interpolated movement to prevent jarring transitions
3.3 Camera Transitions
Section Handoff: Smooth interpolation between section camera positions
Easing Functions: Cubic, exponential, and custom bezier curves
Duration Control: Per-section configurable transition timing
Interrupt Handling: Graceful handling of rapid scroll direction changes
3.4 Viewport Adaptation
Responsive FOV: Adjusts for mobile vs desktop viewports
Safe Zones: Ensures critical content stays within visible bounds
Orientation Change: Handles device rotation on mobile
Scroll-Driven Animation System
The primary mechanism linking user scroll to visual state changes.

4.1 Scroll Tracker
Native Scroll: Listens to window scroll events with passive listeners
Virtual Scroll: Optional smooth-scroll library integration
Progress Calculation: Normalized 0–1 value per section
Velocity Detection: Measures scroll speed for momentum-based effects
4.2 Animation Triggers
Section Entry: Fires when section enters viewport threshold
Section Exit: Fires when section leaves viewport
Progress Milestones: Discrete triggers at defined progress points
Continuous: Smooth interpolation across entire scroll range
4.3 Animation Types
Transform Animations: Position, rotation, scale changes
Material Animations: Opacity, color, roughness, metalness transitions
Camera Animations: FOV shifts, position lerps, target changes
Layout Animations: DOM element positioning and visibility
4.4 Easing & Timing
Cubic Bezier: Custom curves per animation
Spring Physics: Natural-feeling bounce and overshoot
Stagger: Sequential delays for grouped elements
Duration Mapping: Scroll distance to animation duration ratio
4.5 Scroll Snap (Optional)
Snap Points: Defined positions where scroll locks
Snap Type: Proximity-based or mandatory
Duration: Animation time to reach snap point
Easing: Curve applied during snap transition
Editorial Layout System
Manages the structured content sections that compose the immersive page.

5.1 Section Registry
Section Types: Hero, Product Showcase, Story, Gallery, CTA, etc.
Schema Definition: Liquid schema for Shopify theme editor
Default Values: Fallback configuration per section type
Validation: Ensures required fields are populated
5.2 Layout Engine
Stack Model: Vertical stacking of sections with configurable gaps
Full-Bleed Support: Sections that span the entire viewport
Content Width: Constrained vs full-width layout options
Responsive Reflow: Layout adjustments at defined breakpoints
5.3 Content Blocks
Text Blocks: Headings, paragraphs, captions with typography controls
Media Blocks: Images, videos, 3D models with aspect ratio preservation
Interactive Blocks: Buttons, forms, hotspots
Overlay Blocks: Content layered over 3D or media backgrounds
5.4 Typography System
Font Loading: Preloading of custom fonts with fallback strategy
Scale Modular: Consistent type scale across sections
Responsive Sizing: Viewport-relative font sizing
Animation: Text reveal effects (character, word, line)
5.5 Media Handling
Image Optimization: Responsive srcset generation
Lazy Loading: Intersection Observer-based loading
Video Support: Autoplay, muted, loop configurations
3D Model Integration: GLB/GLTF loading with Draco compression
Asset Management
Handles loading, caching, and lifecycle of all media and 3D assets.

6.1 Asset Loader
Texture Loader: Supports PNG, JPG, WebP, AVIF formats
Model Loader: GLB/GLTF with Draco and KTX2 compression
HDR Loader: Environment maps in HDR and EXR formats
Font Loader: WOFF2 with subsetting support
6.2 Loading Strategy
Preload Critical: Above-the-fold assets loaded first
Progressive Loading: Lower quality → higher quality swap
Priority Queue: Section visibility determines load order
Background Loading: Non-critical assets loaded during idle time
6.3 Caching Layer
Browser Cache: Leverages HTTP caching headers
Memory Cache: In-memory store for active scene assets
IndexedDB: Persistent cache for large assets
Cache Invalidation: Version-based cache busting
6.4 Fallback System
Image Fallback: Static image when WebGL fails
Model Fallback: Placeholder geometry for failed 3D loads
Graceful Degradation: Reduced effects on low-end devices
Error Recovery: Retry logic with exponential backoff
Interaction Layer
Manages all user input and interactive behaviors.

7.1 Input Handlers
Mouse/Touch: Unified pointer event handling
Keyboard: Navigation and accessibility support
Gyroscope: Device orientation for mobile parallax
Gamepad: Optional controller input support
7.2 Hotspot System
3D Anchors: Positioned in 3D space, projected to screen
Hover States: Visual feedback on cursor proximity
Click Actions: Navigation, modal open, product quick-view
Tooltip Display: Contextual information on interaction
7.3 Drag & Rotate
Orbit Controls: Click-drag to rotate around focal point
Pan Controls: Shift + drag for lateral movement
Zoom Controls: Scroll wheel or pinch-to-zoom
Inertia: Momentum-based continuation after release
7.4 Gesture Recognition
Swipe: Directional swipe detection
Pinch: Two-finger zoom gesture
Long Press: Extended touch for special actions
Double Tap: Quick zoom or selection
7.5 Accessibility
Keyboard Navigation: Tab-through interactive elements
Screen Reader: ARIA labels and live regions
Reduced Motion: Respects prefers-reduced-motion
Focus Management: Visible focus indicators and logical order
Performance & Optimization
Ensures smooth 60fps experience across devices.

8.1 Performance Budget
Frame Time Target: 16.6ms per frame (60fps)
Draw Call Limit: Maximum draw calls per frame
Texture Memory: GPU memory budget enforcement
Triangle Count: Per-scene polygon budget
8.2 Level of Detail (LOD)
Distance-Based: Swap models based on camera distance
Screen Size: Reduce detail for small on-screen objects
Device Tier: Automatic quality scaling by device capability
Progressive Enhancement: Add detail as performance allows
8.3 Occlusion & Culling
Frustum Culling: Skip rendering off-screen objects
Occlusion Culling: Skip hidden objects behind others
Backface Culling: Skip rendering of inward-facing polygons
Instanced Rendering: Batch identical geometry draws
8.4 Memory Management
Geometry Disposal: Remove unused buffers from GPU
Texture Disposal: Release texture memory on section unload
Material Pooling: Reuse material instances
Garbage Collection: Minimize JS heap allocations in render loop
8.5 Monitoring
FPS Counter: Real-time frame rate display (debug mode)
Memory Profiler: GPU and JS heap tracking
Load Time Metrics: Time to interactive measurement
Error Tracking: Capture and report rendering failures
Theme Integration
Connects the immersive system with Shopify's theme architecture.

9.1 Liquid Integration
Section Files: .liquid files with schema definitions
Snippet Reuse: Shared components via {% include %}
Block System: Nested blocks for flexible content
Preset Configurations: Pre-built section configurations
9.2 Shopify Section API
Dynamic Loading: Load sections via AJAX on navigation
Section Refresh: Update individual sections without full reload
Event Hooks: shopify:section:load, shopify:section:unload
State Persistence: Maintain immersive state across section updates
9.3 Theme Customizer
Color Settings: Background, accent, text colors per section
Animation Controls: Speed, intensity, enable/disable toggles
Layout Options: Width, spacing, alignment controls
Preview Support: Live preview in theme editor
9.4 Metafields Integration
3D Model References: Link products to 3D assets
Animation Presets: Store animation configurations
Content Relationships: Connect editorial content to products
Custom Data: Arbitrary data for specialized behaviors
9.5 Multi-Language Support
Translation Keys: All text content via Shopify translations
RTL Support: Right-to-left layout adaptation
Locale-Aware Formatting: Dates, currencies, units
Font Fallback: Script-appropriate font selection

